    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5814A\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the town of Islip, county of Suffolk, to discontinue\nas parklands and lease certain lands\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAn act to authorize the town of Islip, county of Suffolk, to discontinue\nas parklands and lease certain lands\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the town of Islip to discontinue as parklands and\nto lease at fair market value certain property to J.P. Supreme Caterers,\nInc., d/b/a Nicky's on the Bay for a term not to exceed forty years to\nmake the necessary renovations and operate a fuel dock and restaurant.\n\nSection 2 requires the town of Islip, to dedicate the proceeds from the\nlease toward the acquisition of new parklands and/or capital improve-\nments to existing park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 3 describes the meets & bounds of the property to be alienated.\n\nSection 4 requires that, should the lands described in section three of\nthis act cease to be used for the purposes described in section one of\nthis act, the lease shall terminate and those lands shall revert to the\ntown of Islip for public park and recreational purposes. At the time of\nsuch reversion, the removal of such fuel dock and restaurant shall take\nplace and the property shall be returned to its previous state, consist-\nent with park and recreational purposes.\n\nSection 5 requires the town of Islip to comply with any federal govern-\nment before alienating the parkland.\n\nSection 6 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Islip is the owner of the Bay Shore Marina located at 150 S.\nClinton Ave., Bay Shore. The Town needs to alienate the parcel so they\ncan enter into a lease for the restaurant located on site. The Town has\nalready passed a resolution authorizing the Home Rule Request.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
